#: qt/src/FoldersPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Determines where to save these files.</p><p><span style=\" font-style:italic;\">ROM Folder</span> will always save to the same folder as the ROM.</p><p><span style=\" font-style:italic;\">Config Folder</span> will save to a subfolder of the config folder that is shown. If there is a snes9x.conf file next to your executable, Snes9x will operate in portable mode and the config folder will be the folder the executable is in.</p><p><span style=\" font-style:italic;\">Custom</span> allows you to specify exactly where to save these files.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/EmulationPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Emulates the selected number of frames ahead of the displayed frame, so your input appears to take effect sooner. Reduces input latency at the cost of extra processing every frame.</p><p>One frame is safe for most games; higher values can cause glitches in games that poll input mid-frame.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/SoundPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Game Boy only: hides the volume jump a channel makes when a game rewrites NRx2 while the channel is still enabled (the \"zombie\" glitch). Off = exact hardware behaviour, which clicks on every note in some games.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/SoundPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Master pre-amp applied after the volume percentages. 0 dB is unchanged; boosting can clip loud material.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/SoundPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Pre-amp on the GB side of the SGB mix, applied after its volume percentage. Only active in SGB1/SGB2 BIOS mode.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/SoundPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Pre-amp on the SPC side of the SGB mix, applied after its volume percentage. Only active in SGB1/SGB2 BIOS mode.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/EmulationPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Record File → AVI Recording at twice the SNES resolution (512x448, or 512x478 with overscan shown) so hi-res and interlaced games keep their detail. Doubles the file size.</p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: qt/src/FoldersPanel.ui
msgid "<html><head/><body><p>Setting this to anything other than 0 will save the SRAM (internal game saves) file regularly. If it is set to to 0, it will only save when exiting Snes9x or changing games, and you will lose any progress since the last save if your device crashes.</p></body></html>"
msgstr "<html><head/><body><p>Setting this to anything other than 0 will save the SRAM (internal game saves) file regularly. If it is set to to 0, it will only save when exiting Snes9x or changing games, and you will lose any progress since the last save if your device crashes.</p></body></html>"

